Boot down to 3.4 V, the kernel's own power-off level on units whose dts sets power_off_thresd = <3400> (the
RG351P). With low-battery.patch's 3.1 V, U-Boot started Linux between 3.1 and 3.4 V and rk817-bat powered it off
about ten seconds into boot ("battery voltage is under 3400mV ... power off!", seen on an RG351P): a boot that
dies with no low-battery screen. Here U-Boot shows its low-battery screen instead. Still well under stock 3.53 V.

--- a/board/rockchip/odroidgoa/odroidgoa_power.c
+++ b/board/rockchip/odroidgoa/odroidgoa_power.c
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
 #include <power/fuel_gauge.h>
 #include <odroidgoa_status.h>
 
-#define MIN_VOL_LEVEL	3530	/* 3.53V */
+#define MIN_VOL_LEVEL	3400	/* 3.40V */
 
 #define PWR_LED_GPIO	18	/* GPIO0_C2 */
 #define DC_DET_GPIO	11	/* GPIO0_B3 */
